# The build context is the repository root: the image COPYs bin/otterd and
# bin/otter from it, so the context cannot be narrowed to this directory.
# Everything else is excluded, because a context carrying .git, the test suite
# and local caches makes the build slower and gives the image more inputs than
# it has.
*
!packaging/container/**
# The "./" prefix is load-bearing. Without it these patterns are matched by
# prefix, so "!bin/otter" also matches "bin/otterd" -- and because a later
# negative rule wins, it excluded the daemon the image needs. Anchoring to the
# context root makes each pattern name exactly one file.
!./bin/otterd
!./bin/otter
